1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:01,610
It's me, Eden.

2
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:04,070
I saved you in the storm that day.

3
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:05,370
Again.

4
00:00:07,490 --> 00:00:08,490
It's me, Eden.

5
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:11,160
I saved you in the storm that day.

6
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,040
Again.

7
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:15,500
As I've said before,

8
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,300
Luka's tone should be anxious,
not certain.

9
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:26,390
Why don't we stay
and practice this part a bit more?

10
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:27,640
Director Jung,

11
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,680
we can practice here all night, right?

12
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:34,350
Suit yourselves.

13
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:37,820
Guys!

14
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:41,490
We have a problem!

15
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,610
So your so-called problem...

16
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,410
Is that you're craving
grilled meat so much...

17
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:51,910
This is the problem

18
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:54,170
you meant?

19
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:55,460
Hey, flip the meat! It'll burn.

20
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:55,960
Hurry.

21
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,290
I flip it?

22
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:58,880
Give it to me.

23
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:03,840
Wait, how are you so good at grilling?

24
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,470
I've worked part-time a lot.

25
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:07,890
Hey, see?

26
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:09,970
I'm an expert at picking people.

27
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:12,020
I'm a person too, okay?

28
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:15,520
Come on.

29
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,980
Let's all

30
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,800
toast to "The Mermaid Prince."

31
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,940
Cheers!

32
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:22,900
Am I late?

33
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,620
Oh, Lawyer Yoo, you're here.

34
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:32,830
How've you been?

35
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:33,830
Great, of course.

36
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:37,000
The atmosphere is nice.

37
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:38,960
Right?

38
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,420
It's rare for everyone to be here.

39
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:42,050
Stop drinking.

40
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:43,380
I'm fine.

41
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,759
I'll drink it.

42
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,220
What for?

43
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,590
What for?

44
00:01:53,470 --> 00:01:54,930
What's going on with them?

45
00:01:56,229 --> 00:01:56,940
Quiet.

46
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:11,660
Right, of course

47
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,540
we have to down the first shot.

48
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,290
Everyone, raise your glasses.

49
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:18,710
Cheers!

50
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:27,430
Let me pour you a glass.

51
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:30,260
Sure, I'll have a glass.

52
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
[Hongseok]

53
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:49,950
[Park Seonghyeon]

54
00:02:52,850 --> 00:02:54,850
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

55
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,450
[Play Me]

56
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,200
Wait a minute.

57
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,930
Yeah, hello?

58
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:13,950
Uh-huh.

59
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:17,220
Okay, got it. Okay.

60
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:19,100
Yihyun.

61
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:19,690
Yeah?

62
00:03:19,690 --> 00:03:22,270
Something urgent came up. I have to go.

63
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:23,980
Take care.

64
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:25,440
Take care.

65
00:03:28,990 --> 00:03:31,360
Oh, it's a taxi!

66
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,910
Hey!

67
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,160
I won!

68
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,020
That damn skyscraper...

69
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:44,130
I beat him.

70
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:46,960
I almost drank myself to death.

71
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:57,430
It's impossible to get a taxi.

72
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:03,650
Yihyun.

73
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,690
Don't hate me.

74
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:13,870
Don't push me away, please.

75
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:31,720
What?

76
00:04:33,930 --> 00:04:35,470
This isn't my place.

77
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:02,750
Good morning.

78
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:23,140
Oh, I took your phone to get it repaired.

79
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:26,020
My phone?

80
00:05:26,190 --> 00:05:27,520
Why?

81
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:31,360
I dropped it and it broke.

82
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:33,530
Don't you remember?

83
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,700
My phone's broken?

84
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,800
Hey!

85
00:05:41,409 --> 00:05:43,040
Give me a ride. Right now.

86
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,830
Sorry!

87
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:47,000
I'm really sorry I'm late.

88
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,300
No matter how long it takes,
I'll finish it before I leave.

89
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,340
You can count on me.

90
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:57,640
Well, just help me prep these fabrics.

91
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:58,990
Oh, okay.

92
00:05:59,090 --> 00:06:03,350
By the way, wasn't there supposed
to be another person coming today?

93
00:06:03,350 --> 00:06:06,940
Since you didn't show up,
I told them not to come.

94
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:11,980
So... I have to do all of this by myself?

95
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,850
Didn't you say I could count on you?

96
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:15,740
I'll leave it to you.

97
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:23,200
How can I finish all this by myself?

98
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:45,180
Is this how you wear it?

99
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:47,390
So cute... No,

100
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,600
it really suits you.

101
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,940
Yes, it suits you.

102
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:53,360
I really don't know
why I have to help you.

103
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:56,530
That's irresponsible of you to say.

104
00:06:56,530 --> 00:07:00,200
Who broke my phone?

105
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,800
Who took in a drunk person
when they couldn't find their way home?

106
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:08,370
As they say, many hands make light work.

107
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:30,600
Take this...

108
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:35,510
Brush it out like this.

109
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,100
Hey, hey. What are you doing?

110
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:57,100
You cheeky thing.

111
00:08:38,630 --> 00:08:41,130
Are you out of your mind?

112
00:08:41,669 --> 00:08:44,730
We drifted apart because of this before,
and now again.

113
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:47,140
We're going to drift apart again.

114
00:08:48,010 --> 00:08:49,560
Just now...

115
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,640
Uh, I'm sorry.

116
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,060
No, what I mean is...

117
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:57,940
Uh, I drank a lot yesterday.

118
00:08:57,940 --> 00:09:00,480
And... Oh.

119
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:03,070
I'm also a bit dizzy
from the paint fumes, so...

120
00:09:03,070 --> 00:09:05,110
Kang Jae-on.

121
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:08,870
I like you.

122
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:10,870
I said, I like you.

123
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:12,750
What'd you say?

124
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:15,710
It means what it means.

125
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:21,710
Um, so,

126
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:26,140
what... what is it that you mean?

127
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,390
What'd you say?

128
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,560
Didn't he tell me not to push him away?

129
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,190
That's why I didn't.

130
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:44,030
Since we kissed, I can't say I hate him.

131
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:45,400
So I said I like him.

132
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:50,700
What if he also says he likes me?

133
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:54,910
Fine.

134
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,420
Sure.

135
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:01,710
We're official from today.

136
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:03,010
Hey...

137
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,810
let's pretend yesterday never happened.

138
00:10:16,810 --> 00:10:17,560
Okay!

139
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,900
Huh?

140
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:38,100
[Epilogue]

141
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,670
I said, I like you.

142
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:48,090
All... All I view?

143
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,550
All I knew?

144
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:53,180
What is it that he knew?

145
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:58,190
View... What he views of our kiss?

146
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:01,310
But if I ask him again,

147
00:11:01,310 --> 00:11:04,860
we'll probably drift apart again.

148
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,280
All...
